{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,glob\nfor p in sorted(glob.glob('Tasks/*.yaml')):\n d=json.load(open(p))\n print(f\\\"{d['id']} {d['kind']:<14} {d['execution_scope']:<29} deps={len(d['depends_on']):2} ac={len(d['acceptance_criteria']):2} gates={len(d['completion_gates']):2} {d['title']}\\\")\nPY\nrg -n 'clarif|ambig|playtest|human|exact|tuning|undefined|missing|future|later' Tasks/*.yaml | sed -n '1,280p'\"","aggregated_output":"Tasks/NSC-007.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"GDD Section 2 fully specifies Fireball's tap/charge behavior, cost/restriction relationship, and area-vs-single-target tradeoff; no missing design blocks representing it as one bounded implementation item.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-007.yaml:118:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-009.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"GDD fully specifies Force Wave's radial/player-centered aiming model, cost, cooldown role, and displacement-request ownership split; no missing design blocks a single bounded implementation item.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-009.yaml:31:      \"requirement\": \"Each cast spends 25 mana (initial tuning value) through Player Mana's existing owner-controlled Spend interface and starts Force Wave's own visible long cooldown; the cast is refused if the spend fails.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-009.yaml:73:      \"requirement\": \"Failure caused by using Force Wave without an immediate threat and then lacking it during a later critical moment, due to its long cooldown, is readable to the player.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-009.yaml:108:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-008.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"GDD fully specifies Frost Field's targeting, ownership split (Wizard Combat triggers; Enemy Pursuit applies/restores), and feedback requirement; no missing design blocks a single bounded implementation item.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-008.yaml:32:      \"requirement\": \"Frost Field provides player-facing feedback that makes the cast and the active field readable during placement and while active; the exact visual/audio treatment is an implementation choice.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-008.yaml:100:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-006.yaml:33:  \"notes\": \"Aggregate repository_state is 'missing' because all three represented children (fireball, frost-field, force-wave) are currently unimplemented.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-006.yaml:34:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-010.yaml:41:  \"notes\": \"Aggregate repository_state is missing because none of this domain's represented child work (registry, health/defeat, status-effect/displacement) currently exists anywhere in Assets/. Enemy roster stats, pursuit/attack behavior, and locked-door attack ownership belong to the enemy_behavior domain's nodes (enemy-pursuit-search-foundation, melee-enemy, ranged-enemy, locked-door-enemy-attack) and are intentionally not duplicated here.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-010.yaml:42:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-002.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"Already decomposed into the three concrete owned systems (movement, health, mana) required by the current GDD; no further missing-design problem needs resolving at this organizational level.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-002.yaml:29:  \"notes\": \"Aggregate repository_state of partial reflects that PlayerHealth/PlayerMana/PlayerMovement all exist with real behavior but each is missing GDD-required interfaces (restore, reset, cursor projection, movement-restriction, health UI, denied-cast feedback).\",\r\nTasks/NSC-005.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"Required reset and denied-cast-signal behavior are fully specified by current GDD text without inventing new design; exact feedback presentation is explicitly an implementation choice.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-005.yaml:25:      \"requirement\": \"Exposes a signal (e.g. an event) when a cast attempt is denied due to insufficient mana, distinct from a successful spend, so a consuming spell/UI can present readable low-mana feedback; exact presentation is an implementation choice.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-011.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD fully specifies this capability's contract: what it tracks, the hard cap, register/unregister semantics, what does NOT remove an enemy, and reset participation. No missing design blocks turning this into a bounded implementation item.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-011.yaml:73:      \"requirement\": \"The registry/bookkeeping responsibility is a reusable runtime foundation and does not require the exact five-room encounter layouts, placements, or trigger authoring to be known first.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-011.yaml:88:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-012.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD fully specifies health/damage/defeat ownership, the damage-interface contract, the registry-removal reporting contract, and reset participation. No missing design blocks a bounded implementation item.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-012.yaml:27:      \"requirement\": \"Reaching zero health triggers a defeat transition exactly once for that persistent enemy object.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-012.yaml:54:      \"requirement\": \"Verify a damage source can only reduce a persistent enemy's health through the owner-controlled damage interface and that zero health triggers the defeat transition exactly once.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-012.yaml:105:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-003.yaml:88:  \"notes\": \"Exact movement speed/feel tuning is left to playtesting per GDD and is not part of this item's required acceptance surface.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-004.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"Required restore, death-transition, feedback, and reset behavior are fully specified by current GDD text without inventing new design; exact recovery/damage values are explicitly deferred to playtesting by the GDD itself.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-004.yaml:77:  \"notes\": \"Exact fixed door-lock recovery amount is an explicitly deferred playtesting value per GDD; this item only needs to expose the clamped restore interface, not decide the tuning number.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-019.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD fully specifies click-to-approach selection, arrival-triggered auto-timing, cursor-drift tolerance, and interruption conditions; no missing design remains for this responsibility.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-022.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The organizational grouping itself needs no additional design; its represented children are individually concrete or already resolved to a bounded configuration gap. No missing-design problem blocks bootstrapping this feature.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-022.yaml:33:  \"notes\": \"Aggregate of one implemented child (fixed-isometric-camera) and three missing children (package configuration, navigation/locomotion layer, visual foundation). Does not include five-room content/encounter authoring, which belongs to a separate deferred feature outside this domain.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-021.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD fully specifies close/lock triggering, health-restore request semantics, durability/damage-interface ownership, the locked-to-broken transition, forward-only enforcement, required breach feedback, and navigation-publication ownership; no missing design remains, only implementation bundling.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-021.yaml:131:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-014.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The detection/pursuit/lose-target/search/wander/reacquisition contract, threshold relationship, doorway-traversal rule, and reset participation are already fully specified by the GDD; only exact distance/duration tuning numbers are explicitly deferred to playtesting and do not block building the mechanism.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-014.yaml:103:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-013.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD fully specifies this component's two effect types (Frost slowdown apply/restore; forced displacement apply/restore), the explicit Ranged-Enemy-attack-is-unaffected constraint, the pursuit/search hand-back requirement, and reset participation. No missing design blocks a bounded implementation item; the two effect types are explicitly bundled into one reusable component by GDD Section 5.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-013.yaml:79:      \"requirement\": \"Frost Field slows a ranged enemy's repositioning but does not stop its attacks; the player must still move laterally or use room geometry to avoid incoming shots.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-013.yaml:106:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-020.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD specifies the exact required behavior (detect actual forward-side crossing after open, expose to consumers, participate in reset); the underlying Unity mechanism is an explicit implementation choice, not missing design.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-020.yaml:68:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-017.yaml:67:      \"requirement\": \"The player understands that enemies left alive remain a threat: leaving them alive means locking a door while they attack it, and later encountering them if that door breaks through.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-017.yaml:100:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-023.yaml:43:      \"reference\": \"GDD - Camera completion and future integration\",\r\nTasks/NSC-023.yaml:67:      \"observation\": \"BuildCamera sets camera.orthographic = true, camera.orthographicSize = 8f, and cameraObject.transform.rotation = Quaternion.Euler(30f, -45f, 0f) once; no later code path in the builder modifies camera rotation.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-024.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"This is a bounded project-configuration change (adding two named, already-approved package entries) with no missing design.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-024.yaml:58:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-015.yaml:37:      \"requirement\": \"A retreating player cannot maintain indefinite safety through ordinary movement alone; Melee Enemy pursuit gradually closes distance over time, with exact speed/tuning left to playtesting.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-015.yaml:91:      \"requirement\": \"Melee Enemies gradually close the distance over time; movement alone cannot preserve a completely safe distance indefinitely in later encounters.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-015.yaml:110:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-016.yaml:92:      \"requirement\": \"Ranged Enemy keeps moderate distance and fires a slow telegraphed shot; forces lateral movement while Melee Enemies close in.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-016.yaml:96:      \"requirement\": \"A Ranged Enemy may end up fighting alone if its Melee support is defeated first; tap Fireball, cover, and lateral movement remain effective against a lone survivor.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-016.yaml:104:      \"requirement\": \"Frost Field slows a Ranged Enemy's repositioning but does not stop its attacks; the player must still move laterally or use room geometry to avoid incoming shots.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-016.yaml:115:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-031.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD already specifies the orchestrator's ownership contract and required participants in full; this feature node organizes a staged bootstrap implementation plus a later full-closure implementation without inventing missing design.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-031.yaml:33:  \"notes\": \"Aggregate repository_state of missing reflects that no restart-related code exists in the current repository at all.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-031.yaml:34:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-030.yaml:12:  \"decomposition_state\": \"needs_future_decomposition\",\r\nTasks/NSC-030.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"Exact encounter placements, triggers, per-door durability values, and Final Room pressure composition are explicitly left to later authoring/playtesting by the GDD; only composition/sizing rules (3-8 enemies, never-isolated Ranged Enemy, mixed compositions in two named rooms, Ranged Enemy first introduced in Chapel of Ash) are currently fixed. Inventing exact placements/triggers now would fabricate missing design. Encounter placement/content authoring is a real prerequisite consumer of the room spaces produced by five-room-content-authoring (GDD Section 5 — 2.5D Isometric Visual and World Representation: 'encounter placement/content consumes the authored room spaces and the encounter-admission/cap foundation'); once both features gain concrete descendants, a Progressive Decomposer must attach a concrete encounter-placement -> authored-room implementation/artifact dependency between those descendants rather than a feature-to-feature edge.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-030.yaml:74:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-026.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD already specifies which object categories use Tilemap versus SpriteRenderer, the sorting-convention requirement, and the visual/gameplay separation principle; no missing design blocks scoping this item at the foundation level. Authoring the five actual room layouts remains separately deferred and out of this item's scope.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-026.yaml:79:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-035.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD fully specifies the victory trigger, overlay, and suspend-interface consumption contract; no missing design remains.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-035.yaml:30:      \"requirement\": \"Victory is triggered exactly when the shared doorway-crossing state (owned by Door and Interaction) reports forward-side crossing of the final door; no independent crossing check is implemented.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-035.yaml:75:  \"notes\": \"If a future graph introduces a single shared input-gating owner that centralizes these consumers, victory should depend on that owner instead of duplicating six edges (per prompt guidance); no such owner currently exists.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-035.yaml:76:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-029.yaml:12:  \"decomposition_state\": \"needs_future_decomposition\",\r\nTasks/NSC-029.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"Exact room geometry, dimensions, prop placement, and chokepoint/cover layout for each of the five named spaces are not specified beyond their stated tactical purpose; inventing that geometry now would fabricate missing design. The named-space tactical requirements are preserved as acceptance context for a future Progressive Decomposer rather than resolved here.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-029.yaml:67:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-034.yaml:30:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-033.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD names the complete required participant list and the exact reset contract for full closure; no missing design remains, though most listed owners do not yet exist.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-033.yaml:87:  \"notes\": \"Most of this item's dependencies are currently missing entirely (not merely unfinished), so this item cannot be dispatched meaningfully until the underlying owners exist.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-033.yaml:88:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-032.yaml:46:      \"requirement\": \"Play Mode check: reducing Player Health to zero triggers a fresh floor attempt exactly once per zero-health transition.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-032.yaml:70:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-025.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"The GDD already specifies the approved technology (Unity AI Navigation/NavMesh), the ownership split for the passability interface, and the exact semantic-to-walkability translation rules; no additional design invention is needed to scope this item.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-025.yaml:65:      \"requirement\": \"The approved implementation uses Unity AI Navigation (com.unity.ai.navigation) and NavMesh-based runtime movement; enemy detection/pursuit/search logic does not choose or configure a different navigation technology independently. The exact underlying mechanism for updating doorway passability is an implementation choice.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-025.yaml:79:  \"notes\": \"Exact Detection/Lose Target distances and other tuning values remain GDD-deferred playtesting values and are not part of this item's scope; only the walkable-representation and passability-interface responsibilities belong here.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-025.yaml:80:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-027.yaml:13:  \"decomposition_reason\": \"This is the organizational parent for encounter-admission runtime enforcement and deferred encounter-content authoring; it is not itself a design problem to resolve, so it is coarse rather than needs_future_decomposition.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-027.yaml:34:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-036.yaml:39:  \"notes\": \"Aggregate repository_state of 'missing' reflects that its sole currently-known concrete descendant (windows-build-scene-registration) has confirmed zero registered scenes and no other build-configuration evidence was found. Per the feature-aggregate rule, evidence is kept on the child implementation item rather than duplicated here.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-036.yaml:40:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-028.yaml:67:      \"requirement\": \"The registry tracks active persistent enemies under a hard fifteen-enemy cap; the Dungeon Encounter system consumes the registry before activating new encounter enemies, and if activation would exceed fifteen, new encounter enemies are delayed or reduced first while existing persistent pursuers are never removed to make room. This bookkeeping/admission foundation is explicitly reusable and does not require the exact five-room encounter layouts, placements, or trigger authoring to be known first.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-028.yaml:71:      \"requirement\": \"Surviving enemies carry forward and combine with later encounters as the same persistent enemy objects, not new spawns, and the game never permits more than fifteen active enemies at once.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-028.yaml:81:  \"notes\": \"Must not be folded into or blocked by dungeon-encounter-content-authoring's needs_future_decomposition status; this is the 'known runtime behavior' half of the split required by the reconciliation guidance.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-028.yaml:82:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\nTasks/NSC-037.yaml:11:  \"execution_reason\": \"Registering one named scene and configuring the Windows Standalone build target is a bounded project-configuration change one agent can perform; the required human inspection of the result afterward is a separate pipeline gate (see 'Human inspection and final integration authority'), not an execution-scope split.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-037.yaml:22:      \"requirement\": \"The canonical gameplay scene (currently Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity, or a later human-approved replacement) is registered in Unity Build Settings.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-037.yaml:52:      \"requirement\": \"The current canonical gameplay scene is Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity; that scene (or a later human-approved replacement) must be registered in Unity Build Settings before the Windows delivery requirement can be considered complete. A committed EditorBuildSettings.asset with no registered canonical gameplay scene is confirmed incomplete build configuration. The top-level Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity and Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity stubs do not satisfy this requirement merely because they are .unity files.\"\r\nTasks/NSC-037.yaml:58:  \"notes\": \"Do not repurpose the non-canonical Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity or Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity stubs to satisfy this item; per the GDD's Current Prototype Scene Evidence section and the 'Non-canonical prototype scene preservation' pipeline constraint, their disposition is a separate human decision.\",\r\nTasks/NSC-037.yaml:59:  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"missing\",\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
